02:29.040 --> 02:38.040
Feature, update, Pokedex to be almost fully composition API.

02:38.040 --> 02:40.560
OK.

02:40.560 --> 02:42.720
So what is script setup?

02:42.720 --> 02:45.080
Well, script setup is exactly as it sounds,

02:45.080 --> 02:47.480
in that what you do is you add an attribute

02:47.480 --> 02:49.920
to your script block called setup.

02:49.920 --> 02:51.680
And what that does is it tells you

02:51.680 --> 02:54.960
this entire block is going to be composition API.

02:54.960 --> 02:57.240
Like, no options will exist in here.

02:57.240 --> 02:58.440
So what does that mean?

02:58.440 --> 03:00.520
Well, first thing first, there's no more objects.

03:00.520 --> 03:02.760
That's what options API is all about,

03:02.760 --> 03:04.000
about defining this object.

03:04.000 --> 03:07.800
So export default disappears.

03:07.800 --> 03:08.920
Then we can save that.

03:08.920 --> 03:10.440
But that's still going to break, which is totally fine,

03:10.440 --> 03:11.480
because you know why?

03:11.480 --> 03:13.080
We already know that it's in setup.

03:13.080 --> 03:15.120
So line five, this async setup here,

03:15.120 --> 03:16.360
also not necessary.

03:16.360 --> 03:18.840
Delete.

03:18.840 --> 03:20.040
Save.

03:20.040 --> 03:20.880
Better.

03:20.880 --> 03:24.360
But here's the other thing.

03:24.360 --> 03:26.200
Because we're now in a compiler optimization,

03:26.200 --> 03:29.160
meaning view can now do a lot more static analysis

03:29.160 --> 03:30.920
and those sort of things, we don't even

03:30.920 --> 03:32.400
need to return anything either.

03:35.600 --> 03:38.520
And believe it or not, this block of code here, in fact,

03:38.520 --> 03:41.320
let me just delete the console logs here,

03:41.320 --> 03:43.640
this is whole thing just works.

03:43.640 --> 03:47.040
It just sold me.

03:47.040 --> 03:50.200
I was super skeptical until this moment.

03:50.200 --> 03:53.240
Yeah, this is the mic drop moment for those who are thinking

03:53.240 --> 03:55.040
about composition API.

03:55.040 --> 03:58.840
This is, this makes a lot of people excited,

03:58.840 --> 04:00.320
especially for those users who are heavier

04:00.320 --> 04:01.320
on the JavaScript side.

04:01.320 --> 04:04.240
Or more importantly, if you're even thinking about TypeScript,

04:04.240 --> 04:07.800
composition API works with TypeScript like naturally,

04:07.800 --> 04:10.120
in terms of annotating types and all that stuff.

04:10.120 --> 04:11.680
We don't have time to talk about this today,

04:11.680 --> 04:14.080
but there's a View3 and TypeScript workshop that just

04:14.080 --> 04:15.120
actually released recently.

04:15.120 --> 04:16.440
So if you want to check that out to learn more

04:16.440 --> 04:17.920
about how that might work together,

04:17.920 --> 04:20.560
you can totally check that out.

04:20.560 --> 04:21.520
But there you go.

04:21.520 --> 04:23.800
This is how you get a component to fully opt

04:23.800 --> 04:26.520
into composition API while not having to worry

04:26.520 --> 04:28.600
about any of the eight.

04:28.600 --> 04:30.640
One of the things actually that you might be thinking though

04:30.640 --> 04:33.360
is that we had an async earlier on our setup.

04:33.360 --> 04:35.120
But when you're in the script setup,

04:35.120 --> 04:38.320
basically view, hoist, and does all the async stuff for you

04:38.320 --> 04:40.880
so that you don't have to manually assign it here.

04:40.880 --> 04:42.560
It'll automatically detect the async stuff

04:42.560 --> 04:44.520
and do what it needs to do.

04:44.520 --> 04:47.640
And so just like that, we now have a component that's fully

04:47.640 --> 04:49.600
opted into composition API.

04:49.600 --> 04:51.400
No options anywhere.

04:51.400 --> 04:54.040
The only thing I will add is because this probably

04:54.040 --> 04:56.320
wouldn't be the most intuitive, is that let's say we wanted

04:56.320 --> 04:59.520
to add our base button inside of this layout.

04:59.520 --> 05:02.320
All we do is you do base button.

05:02.320 --> 05:07.800
We import it into this base button.

05:07.800 --> 05:09.920
And believe it or not, just by importing it,

05:09.960 --> 05:11.080
you've already registered it.

05:11.080 --> 05:16.040
So I can come down in here now and just go base button like that.

05:16.040 --> 05:17.600
You can see there's our base button.

05:20.680 --> 05:22.640
