05:48.520 --> 05:52.320
And spaghetti code can become very problematic very quickly.

05:52.320 --> 05:53.920
Again, one of the things I want to emphasize

05:53.920 --> 05:56.200
is that there are trade-offs when you go the options route

05:56.200 --> 05:58.120
versus the composition API route.

05:58.120 --> 05:59.560
And understanding those trade-offs

05:59.560 --> 06:01.600
are, if we think about it, are what make us experience

06:01.600 --> 06:02.600
as engineers.

06:02.600 --> 06:03.800
And so knowing that, you just have

06:03.800 --> 06:05.720
to realize that composition API means there's

06:05.720 --> 06:07.160
flexibility and freedom.

06:07.160 --> 06:09.400
And so your team has to then design the conventions it's

06:09.400 --> 06:11.560
going to use in order to make sure that your code is still

06:11.560 --> 06:13.920
maintainable and readable.

06:13.920 --> 06:16.040
As much as options API was a little bit rigid,

06:16.040 --> 06:17.680
as far as telling you where to put stuff,

06:17.680 --> 06:20.000
it did mean everyone knew where everything was at any point.

06:20.000 --> 06:21.760
